<div class="hub-intro" style="padding-top:2rem"><p>The NFL Scouting Combine puts more than 300 draft prospects through the same tests every year: the 40-yard dash, vertical jump, broad jump, 3-cone drill, 20-yard shuttle and 225-pound bench press, plus height, weight, arm length and hand size.</p><p>Because every prospect runs the same tests, the results make a common yardstick for athleticism. Relative Athletic Score (RAS) rolls them into one 0 to 10 number by position. The numbers don&#x27;t decide careers on their own, but they explain a lot about who gets drafted early and which players can survive the physical demands of each position.</p></div>
